<pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Iee10295096249d0c72c29077c89d0d3b73625636" commit="263fc760c73b61633f1aa26825139461dab7a61d" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: rockchip: i2s: rename I2S_CKR_TRCM_TX/RXSHARE to I2S_CKR_TRCM_TX/RXONLY  this patch make it more reasonable and readable, because when we chose I2S_CKR_TRCM_TXONLY, we only output clk_lrck_tx, and hardware need to confirm this signal is wired to external codec lrck_tx/rx at the same time.  for convenience, we just handle lrck_txonly if we enable symmetric_rates in driver and dai_link. otherwise, we use the separate lrck_tx/rx.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52172 TEST=I2S0_LRCK_RX output waveform when capture  Change-Id: Iee10295096249d0c72c29077c89d0d3b73625636 Signed-off-by: Sugar Zhang &lt;sugar.zhang@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (cherry picked from git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/broonie/sound.git linuxsound/topic/rockchip  commit 7ec4a1c34a190297540626dfa240dc033beca196) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346856 " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346856" owner_email="zhengxing@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/56/346856/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I185bd7a110e850667dcf5e166ebb54175af007af" commit="69856f8233f8545e8a23b53691e3e8f22c328c96" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: da7219: Update PLL ranges and dividers to improve locking  The expected MCLK frequency ranges and the associated dividers are updated to improve PLL locking in a corner scenario, with low MCLK frequency near an input divider change boundary.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52172 TEST=codec can be loaded  Signed-off-by: Adam Thomson &lt;Adam.Thomson.Opensource@diasemi.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 63a450aa4d08ccf4f53e9fa59144e746e2288319)  Change-Id: I185bd7a110e850667dcf5e166ebb54175af007af Signed-off-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346857 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346857" owner_email="zhengxing@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/57/346857/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I7ba36c6b903e69a3baf49b9e97965c7a86e08e70" commit="d5a92c2ada753eb43db8cb772e9d925ae5c50559" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: da7219: Disallow unsupported 32KHz clock setting in set_dai_sysclk()  The PLL function was updated to disallow 32KHz in commit 501f72e9c520 (&quot;ASoC: da7219: Remove support for 32KHz PLL mode&quot;), but set_dai_sysclk() was missed and still permits it. This patch resolves that discrepancy.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52172 TEST=codec can be loaded  Signed-off-by: Adam Thomson &lt;Adam.Thomson.Opensource@diasemi.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit fb137ba64a6415ddf231495f6d1a82de1cd69ed0)  Change-Id: I7ba36c6b903e69a3baf49b9e97965c7a86e08e70 Signed-off-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346858 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346858" owner_email="zhengxing@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/58/346858/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I8e9763d0ff8ebdee1147341e265d0b5a0898d8e8" commit="86a6014deb16d2b13a181452b76407b1283438c9" commit_message="UPSTREAM: ASoC: rt5514: add rt5514 codec driver  This is the initial codec driver for rt5514. The codec includes a low power DSP for voice wake up. The register address is incremental by 4 in the DSP memory map. In order to recover the codec settings in the codec mode and manipulate the DSP mode for voice wake up, we use the multi-level register map. One is for ALSA API in codec mode that can be recovered by cache before recording. Another is for DSP related settings that can be accessed with 32bit address of the DSP in the application of voice wake up.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:52172 TEST=codec can be loaded  Signed-off-by: Oder Chiou &lt;oder_chiou@realtek.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Brown &lt;broonie@kernel.org&gt; (cherry picked from commit 4a6180ea7399b945cd380dc63e2e8118f9b432d3)  Change-Id: I8e9763d0ff8ebdee1147341e265d0b5a0898d8e8 Signed-off-by: Xing Zheng &lt;zhengxing@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/346859 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="346859" owner_email="zhengxing@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/59/346859/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I6b8dc9d7303f123804aaee633b19f1b76dc04a2b" commit="23c0745d5b0c92cd130f07aaf57be5e45c6befe7" commit_message="CHROMIUM: sdhci: tegra: restore clock after setting tap  SD clock enable is being cleared (again) instead of turned back on after setting tap values.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54426 TEST=System boot  Change-Id: I6b8dc9d7303f123804aaee633b19f1b76dc04a2b Signed-off-by: Christopher Freeman &lt;cfreeman@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/347066 Reviewed-by: Puneet Kumar &lt;pu